tel 1.0 specification.tel/tels:1.0.0
name registry

# Draft TEL schema for registry.tel (fury.md §7; formerly universes.tel), the
# machine-readable registry whose prose precursor is design/catalog.md: forms,
# parameters, presumption kinds, tools, host-contract families and the schemas the
# tool ships. One document; each built-in tool's descriptor is a sibling
# <name>.tool.tel under tool.schema.tel, referenced by name. Edge kinds are not
# stored — compiler, egress, join and packaging derive from the node kinds at an
# edge's ends (builds.md §14.2). Extension is by published layers under this same
# schema, merged additively; a later layer redefining an entry is a lint.

scalar Form
  description  A registered form name (builds.md §14.1), possibly with a <parameter> placeholder
  validate     form

scalar DisciplineId
  description  A discipline identifier, e.g. tasty/1 (spec §11.1)
  validate     discipline-id

scalar ModuleRef
  description  A <domain>/<name> index coordinate
  validate     module-ref

scalar Path
  description  A /-separated file path
  validate     path

# --- Forms -----------------------------------------------------------------------

record Source
  description  A source form and the file extensions inferred to it (builds.md §14.4)

  field name Form
  field extension Identifier optional repeatable

record Carrier
  description  An interface-bearing artifact kind within a universe, and its discipline

  field name Identifier
  field discipline DisciplineId

record Universe
  description  A form whose content composes, with its carriers

  field name Form
  field carrier Carrier optional repeatable

# A closed form paired with a host contract (universes.md §1); a parameterized family
# names its parameter, bound by backward flow (builds.md §15.2).
record Deliverable
  field name Form
  field format Identifier
  field host ModuleRef
  field parameter Identifier optional

# --- Parameters -------------------------------------------------------------------

record Parameter
  description  A parameter domain, `parameter <name>`, listing its values

  field name Identifier
  field value Identifier optional repeatable

record Mapping
  description  A platform↔triple correspondence used by the backward flow

  field platform Identifier
  field triple Identifier

# --- Presumption kinds -------------------------------------------------------------

record Kind
  description  A presumption kind word and the discipline governing it (many-to-one)

  field name Identifier
  field discipline DisciplineId

# --- Tools ------------------------------------------------------------------------

record Tool
  description  A built-in tool, `tool <name> <descriptor>`, its descriptor a sibling .tool.tel

  field name Identifier
  field descriptor Path

# A LIRA-distributed tool family (fury.md §6): a built-in name resolves to a coordinate
# whose release is chosen by a rule over the locked version of another tool — `scalac`
# to the Fever family by compiler version.
record Family
  description  A distributed tool family, `family <name> <coordinate>`, and its selection rule

  field name Identifier
  field coordinate ModuleRef
  field by Identifier optional

# --- Host contracts ---------------------------------------------------------------

record Host
  description  A host-contract family with its default steward and tag scheme (hosts.md §3)

  field name Identifier
  field steward String optional
  field tags String optional

# --- Schemas ----------------------------------------------------------------------

record Schema
  description  A TEL schema the tool ships, with its published coordinate

  field name Identifier
  field file Path
  field coordinate ModuleRef optional

document
  field source Source optional repeatable
  field universe Universe optional repeatable
  field deliverable Deliverable optional repeatable
  field parameter Parameter optional repeatable
  field mapping Mapping optional repeatable
  field kind Kind optional repeatable
  field tool Tool optional repeatable
  field family Family optional repeatable
  field host Host optional repeatable
  field schema Schema optional repeatable
